1
00:00:11,022 --> 00:00:15,943
THE ROTTEN EGG HATCHES

2
00:00:16,026 --> 00:00:18,070
HERBIVORE DRAMA CLUB
CARNIVORE DRAMA CLUB

3
00:00:18,154 --> 00:00:21,240
[Bill] So... we got word from the Festival
of the Meteor Committee yesterday.

4
00:00:21,991 --> 00:00:23,117
And, uh...

5
00:00:23,909 --> 00:00:26,287
"The plan to segregate
carnivores and herbivores

6
00:00:26,370 --> 00:00:28,247
between halves of the performance

7
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:31,876
clearly contradicts
our 'Live Together' theme,

8
00:00:31,959 --> 00:00:34,211
our main deciding factor in this decision.

9
00:00:34,795 --> 00:00:39,425
Unfortunately, we are unable to feature
your club at this year's festival."

10
00:00:39,508 --> 00:00:41,469
- What? That's not fair.
- It really says that?

11
00:00:41,552 --> 00:00:43,179
What a cruel thing. I can't believe it.

12
00:00:43,262 --> 00:00:47,641
So that's it then. They're letting
a drama club tradition die.

13
00:00:47,725 --> 00:00:50,644
How sad. And there's nothing we can do?

14
00:00:50,728 --> 00:00:52,229
Uh... [sighs]

15
00:00:52,313 --> 00:00:54,982
[Kai] Come on, Bill!
You can't be okay with this.

16
00:00:55,066 --> 00:00:58,569
If we let them cancel the festival,
we'll never be able to face Louis again.

17
00:00:58,652 --> 00:00:59,737
[sighs] You're right.

18
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:02,490
[Els] Wait a second.
None of this is Bill's fault.

19
00:01:02,573 --> 00:01:03,407
[all sigh]

20
00:01:03,491 --> 00:01:06,202
- [Juno] I don't blame Bill.
- [Kai] Guess it can't be helped.

21
00:01:06,285 --> 00:01:08,913
- But it still sucks.
- Excuse me! Can I say something?

22
00:01:11,749 --> 00:01:12,666
You got this.

23
00:01:14,251 --> 00:01:18,214
I think maybe we made the wrong decision
about the drama club.

24
00:01:18,297 --> 00:01:19,590
What do mean by that?

25
00:01:19,673 --> 00:01:21,717
You remember how we took that vote,

26
00:01:21,801 --> 00:01:24,303
whether we should split ourselves
into two separate clubs

27
00:01:24,386 --> 00:01:26,263
or suspend activities entirely?

28
00:01:26,972 --> 00:01:30,518
[Bill] <i>Yeah. And we chose
to continue activities separately</i>

29
00:01:30,601 --> 00:01:33,896
<i>while not forgetting our aim
of co-existence and co-prosperity.</i>

30
00:01:33,979 --> 00:01:35,439
<i>You know, "living together"?</i>

31
00:01:35,523 --> 00:01:37,817
[scoffs] <i>You'd think
they'd appreciate the effort.</i>

32
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:42,029
It's not so bad. Sure we've got this wall,
but at least they won't shut us down.

33
00:01:42,113 --> 00:01:46,117
[Kibi] Okay, but will there be a wall
to separate carnivores and herbivores

34
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,410
at the venue
for the Festival of the Meteor?

35
00:01:48,494 --> 00:01:51,247
I seriously doubt it.
Why would they have one?

36
00:01:51,330 --> 00:01:53,249
How can they tell us to live together,

37
00:01:53,332 --> 00:01:56,043
but shut us down for integrating
the only way we can?

38
00:01:56,669 --> 00:02:00,756
I mean, I figure the school
just doesn't want to take any more risks.

39
00:02:01,966 --> 00:02:05,928
Safety issue. Anything can happen.
We know that.

40
00:02:06,011 --> 00:02:07,179
[Els sighs]

41
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:10,558
[sighs] Okay, listen.

42
00:02:10,641 --> 00:02:13,936
You all remember the accident.
I lost my arm completely.

43
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:15,980
[all gasp]

44
00:02:16,981 --> 00:02:18,440
[Kibi] <i>When I was in the hospital,</i>

45
00:02:18,524 --> 00:02:21,777
<i>I thought about quitting drama club
and leaving school altogether.</i>

46
00:02:22,403 --> 00:02:25,739
<i>Just seeing a carnivore
made me panic and freeze up.</i>

47
00:02:25,823 --> 00:02:27,658
<i>I felt like I couldn't breathe.</i>

48
00:02:28,409 --> 00:02:29,660
[Tao sighs]

49
00:02:29,743 --> 00:02:32,621
When I was recovering
after they reattached my arm,

50
00:02:33,164 --> 00:02:37,334
<i>I had to stay sitting up in bed,
just staring at my own hand for hours.</i>

51
00:02:37,418 --> 00:02:38,544
[mellow music playing]

52
00:02:38,627 --> 00:02:41,255
<i>The sun and the breeze
came through my window</i>

53
00:02:41,338 --> 00:02:43,048
<i>and brushed up against me,</i>

54
00:02:43,132 --> 00:02:46,427
<i>and very slowly, I started to get feeling
back in my hand.</i>

55
00:02:47,678 --> 00:02:51,640
<i>That was really exciting.
I couldn't wait to touch something.</i>

56
00:02:51,724 --> 00:02:54,894
And I knew exactly who
I wanted to be there for it.

57
00:02:56,729 --> 00:02:58,439
- My friend, Tao.
- [gasps softly]

58
00:02:59,773 --> 00:03:03,819
My point is, it's not like I chose
to have such a fragile body.

59
00:03:03,903 --> 00:03:06,280
Just like Tao didn't choose to be strong.

60
00:03:06,363 --> 00:03:07,239
[Tao exhales]

61
00:03:08,324 --> 00:03:12,077
When I came for that visit
and you asked me to touch your hand...

62
00:03:12,995 --> 00:03:13,829
[sighs]

63
00:03:14,914 --> 00:03:16,123
...I started to cry.

64
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:20,085
<i>Because I knew
that was all way harder on you,</i>

65
00:03:20,169 --> 00:03:22,129
<i>but, still, you considered my feelings.</i>

66
00:03:23,297 --> 00:03:27,092
And that's all it took to take down
the wall that formed between us.

67
00:03:27,176 --> 00:03:28,761
[exhales softly]

68
00:03:28,844 --> 00:03:32,431
It wasn't hard, because I know
who the real Tao is.

69
00:03:33,098 --> 00:03:36,393
A fellow drama club member,
who was always on my side.

70
00:03:36,977 --> 00:03:38,771
[Tao grunts softly]

71
00:03:43,150 --> 00:03:44,860
I think Kibi is right.

72
00:03:44,944 --> 00:03:47,446
We were mistaken.
We shouldn't have listened to the school

73
00:03:47,529 --> 00:03:49,114
- and their idiotic rules.
- [Bill] Tao...

74
00:03:49,198 --> 00:03:52,409
Separating ourselves,
not seeing, not touching.

75
00:03:52,993 --> 00:03:56,330
That might give some of you
peace of mind, but not me!

76
00:03:56,413 --> 00:03:58,999
Now that we've experienced
the dangerous issues

77
00:03:59,083 --> 00:04:00,542
between both of our species,

78
00:04:00,626 --> 00:04:02,503
we've more perspective on the matter.

79
00:04:03,003 --> 00:04:05,297
Yeah, that's all well and good,

80
00:04:05,381 --> 00:04:07,549
but we're not gonna get 'em to bend
on the festival.

81
00:04:07,633 --> 00:04:08,509
It's already over.

82
00:04:08,592 --> 00:04:09,885
No, it is not!

83
00:04:10,427 --> 00:04:13,889
Just look around. We've overcome
way bigger obstacles than this.

84
00:04:13,973 --> 00:04:17,142
Yeah, he's right.
Remember last year's festival?

85
00:04:17,226 --> 00:04:21,188
When I heard that Louis had disappeared,
I thought we'd have to cancel outright,

86
00:04:21,272 --> 00:04:23,691
but then Juno took charge
and it all worked out in the end.

87
00:04:23,774 --> 00:04:26,318
Oh, Ellen.
That wasn't just me, it was all of us.

88
00:04:26,402 --> 00:04:28,570
Right? It's literally that easy.

89
00:04:28,654 --> 00:04:30,990
We pulled it off
because we were all together.

90
00:04:31,573 --> 00:04:34,576
Exactly. We may all have
different positions on this,

91
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:37,871
but we know what we can accomplish
by working together.

92
00:04:37,955 --> 00:04:39,164
So why stop now?

93
00:04:39,748 --> 00:04:42,126
He's right, you know. We're unstoppable.

94
00:04:42,209 --> 00:04:44,962
Yeah. Actors, sound crew,

95
00:04:45,045 --> 00:04:46,839
lighting, the set design...

96
00:04:46,922 --> 00:04:50,592
As long as everyone is committed
to their roles like any other production,

97
00:04:50,676 --> 00:04:53,887
we can create a unified performance,
even with this wall!

98
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:56,432
He's right. It's not hard!

99
00:04:56,515 --> 00:04:59,143
We'll just build a show
the festival committee can't turn down.

100
00:04:59,226 --> 00:05:00,352
Whoa, Els, cool it!

101
00:05:00,936 --> 00:05:03,355
Let's try again!
We'll talk to the committee right now.

102
00:05:03,439 --> 00:05:05,107
- And the school!
- I don't know about that.

103
00:05:05,190 --> 00:05:06,692
[Kai] Yes, you do.

104
00:05:06,775 --> 00:05:08,944
You turn into a housecat
while we weren't looking?

105
00:05:09,028 --> 00:05:11,155
- [Bill] Hey.
- Get it through your thick skull.

106
00:05:11,238 --> 00:05:13,574
Louis choose you as the next president
for a reason.

107
00:05:13,657 --> 00:05:16,035
That's true.
What do you want to do here, Bill?

108
00:05:16,118 --> 00:05:17,536
[splutters]

109
00:05:18,203 --> 00:05:20,456
[exhales] Well, I...

110
00:05:21,832 --> 00:05:24,043
[grunts] Let's do it!

111
00:05:24,126 --> 00:05:26,211
Leave negotiations with the school to me!

112
00:05:26,295 --> 00:05:28,630
- [all cheer]
- [Ellen] That's our Bill!

113
00:05:28,714 --> 00:05:30,716
All right! I'm all in too!

114
00:05:30,799 --> 00:05:33,385
My dad always said,
"There's no nut that can't be cracked!"

115
00:05:33,969 --> 00:05:35,512
You can't even crack a nut.

116
00:05:35,596 --> 00:05:38,557
Hey, I'm going to get it one day.
Just wait.

117
00:05:46,523 --> 00:05:49,193
JUNGLE THEATER

118
00:05:49,318 --> 00:05:50,736
CLOSED TODAY

119
00:05:50,819 --> 00:05:52,863
[Legoshi] <i>Oh, boy.</i>

120
00:05:53,447 --> 00:05:55,365
<i>This place? Really?</i>

121
00:06:07,086 --> 00:06:07,920
<i>Hmm.</i>

122
00:06:12,424 --> 00:06:15,803
I have to assume that you've never been
to a strip show before.

123
00:06:15,886 --> 00:06:17,262
[Legoshi] No, I never have.

124
00:06:17,763 --> 00:06:20,808
Appetite and sexual desire
satisfied at once.

125
00:06:20,891 --> 00:06:23,352
You can see how they're popular
among carnivores.

126
00:06:23,811 --> 00:06:26,063
That's not why you brought me here, is it?

127
00:06:26,146 --> 00:06:28,982
No, I want you to meet
one of the dancers who works here.

128
00:06:31,318 --> 00:06:33,195
She is an okapi.

129
00:06:33,278 --> 00:06:35,572
Herbivores work in the Black Market?

130
00:06:35,656 --> 00:06:39,701
This young lady will be dancing
at Melon's masquerade party later tonight.

131
00:06:40,244 --> 00:06:44,498
And you will be going in undercover
disguised as Haruo, her chaperone.

132
00:06:44,581 --> 00:06:46,625
What? And you picked that name 'cause...

133
00:06:46,708 --> 00:06:49,461
Melon is a male in his mid-twenties
to early-thirties.

134
00:06:49,545 --> 00:06:52,589
The upper half of his face
is that of a gazelle,

135
00:06:52,673 --> 00:06:55,175
but the rest is leopard, very distinctive.

136
00:06:55,259 --> 00:06:58,470
Yeah, I'm sure, but how do we spot him
if he's wearing a mask?

137
00:06:58,554 --> 00:07:00,681
You can leave finding him to me.

138
00:07:00,764 --> 00:07:03,058
But I want you to take him down once I do.

139
00:07:03,809 --> 00:07:05,894
Gohin always knew
how to hold his own in a fight.

140
00:07:05,978 --> 00:07:07,688
I imagine he taught you well.

141
00:07:07,771 --> 00:07:10,482
You really seem to know everything
about me.

142
00:07:10,566 --> 00:07:12,484
Oh, and about your devouring record...

143
00:07:13,235 --> 00:07:15,737
I can make that disappear,
wipe the slate clean.

144
00:07:15,821 --> 00:07:16,864
Huh?

145
00:07:16,947 --> 00:07:20,117
You still want to marry that rabbit, Haru,
isn't that the case?

146
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,160
Um, well, I...

147
00:07:21,910 --> 00:07:25,456
- All right, see you at the party.
- Oh, what? We're not going together?

148
00:07:25,539 --> 00:07:26,707
[yelps]

149
00:07:26,790 --> 00:07:28,917
[suspenseful music playing]

150
00:07:29,001 --> 00:07:30,752
[grunting]

151
00:07:32,921 --> 00:07:34,798
I'll relay instructions through this.

152
00:07:34,882 --> 00:07:36,300
[groans]

153
00:07:37,217 --> 00:07:39,011
- Fine.
- [door opens]

154
00:07:39,928 --> 00:07:42,055
- [Cosmo] Hey, are you Haruo?
- [door closes]

155
00:07:42,139 --> 00:07:42,973
What?

156
00:07:43,056 --> 00:07:44,683
Uh...

157
00:07:44,766 --> 00:07:45,893
Oh. Yes, I am!

158
00:07:45,976 --> 00:07:48,729
Wow, look at you. All business today, huh?

159
00:07:48,812 --> 00:07:50,147
Huh?

160
00:07:50,230 --> 00:07:54,193
[Yahya] <i>And by the way, I've introduced
you to your charge for the evening.</i>

161
00:07:54,276 --> 00:07:58,322
<i>You're a playboy type with a fascination
for underworld parties.</i>

162
00:07:59,323 --> 00:08:01,909
<i>Act well your part, drama club boy.</i>

163
00:08:01,992 --> 00:08:04,536
- You know I only did lighting, right?
- <i>Don't speak out loud!</i>

164
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:05,621
[Legoshi] Oh!

165
00:08:05,704 --> 00:08:08,415
[Yahya] <i>And definitely don't mention
the investigation.</i>

166
00:08:08,499 --> 00:08:10,209
<i>You'll put the ladies in danger.</i>

167
00:08:10,959 --> 00:08:12,002
<i>Now look at my seat.</i>

168
00:08:13,629 --> 00:08:15,464
<i>Put that on before you go inside.</i>

169
00:08:16,507 --> 00:08:18,383
- [Cosmo] Let's go.
- Uh, 'kay.

170
00:08:19,551 --> 00:08:23,180
Uh, hold on, baby!
[softly] "Baby"? Really?

171
00:08:28,185 --> 00:08:29,311
[exhales]

172
00:08:29,895 --> 00:08:31,104
- [door opens]
- Hmm?

173
00:08:33,232 --> 00:08:34,316
Oh, this is Luna.

174
00:08:35,234 --> 00:08:37,778
Hey, gorgeous. Nice to meet ya!

175
00:08:37,861 --> 00:08:40,405
Stop. Don't be weird.
Just be quiet, like a manager should.

176
00:08:40,489 --> 00:08:41,323
Okay.

177
00:08:41,406 --> 00:08:44,409
Don't bully him. Just get in already.

178
00:08:46,537 --> 00:08:49,081
[engine revving]

179
00:08:50,082 --> 00:08:53,544
Now, Haruo, don't think this means
you're invited to this party, okay?

180
00:08:53,627 --> 00:08:55,587
Yeah, I know, that's fine.

181
00:08:55,671 --> 00:08:59,007
- Will there be celebrities?
- Asking about the guests is prohibited.

182
00:08:59,091 --> 00:09:01,218
This is a secret party
for the upper class.

183
00:09:01,301 --> 00:09:03,720
Blow it, and you'll be out
before you can say "Jack Russell."

184
00:09:03,804 --> 00:09:05,347
It'll be crazy fun, though.

185
00:09:05,430 --> 00:09:07,975
Oh, yeah, fun doesn't
even begin to cover it.

186
00:09:08,058 --> 00:09:10,394
I will warn you about one thing.

187
00:09:10,477 --> 00:09:13,188
Anyone hands you a red juice,
just get rid of it.

188
00:09:13,272 --> 00:09:16,191
That stuff will send a weakling like you
right over the edge in no time.

189
00:09:16,275 --> 00:09:17,568
Over the edge?

190
00:09:17,651 --> 00:09:20,362
What she's saying is,
your instincts will take control.

191
00:09:20,445 --> 00:09:23,824
My instincts? Like, I'll want to eat
fresh meat, or what?

192
00:09:23,907 --> 00:09:27,411
The types that come to these parties
have all long since passed that stage.

193
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:31,248
The carnivores at these events
have their impulses under control,

194
00:09:31,331 --> 00:09:34,293
and, generally speaking,
the herbivores are less wary of us.

195
00:09:34,376 --> 00:09:37,045
That's what makes these things
so much fun.

196
00:09:37,129 --> 00:09:39,881
Carnivores and herbivores
truly feel equal.

197
00:09:40,382 --> 00:09:43,343
It's liberation from the constraints
of polite society.

198
00:09:43,927 --> 00:09:46,096
It's the ideal coexistence.

199
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:49,850
That said, there are impulses
far more terrifying

200
00:09:49,933 --> 00:09:52,102
than the urge to eat a steak
every once in a while.

201
00:09:52,185 --> 00:09:53,395
- Huh?
- [chuckles]

202
00:09:53,478 --> 00:09:57,065
Yeah, apparently someone goes missing
at every one of these things.

203
00:09:57,149 --> 00:09:58,358
[stutters] Ah!

204
00:09:58,442 --> 00:10:01,903
So the red juice, is it like...
Is it some kind of drug?

205
00:10:01,987 --> 00:10:05,365
Don't know. But you're not going to
touch it anyway, so who cares?

206
00:10:05,907 --> 00:10:08,160
Now, get those horns on, and keep quiet.

207
00:10:08,243 --> 00:10:09,077
Huh.

208
00:10:14,291 --> 00:10:15,500
[yawns]

209
00:10:23,759 --> 00:10:26,303
- Good evening.
- Thanks for working the door.

210
00:10:29,014 --> 00:10:30,015
[groans]

211
00:10:30,557 --> 00:10:34,436
<i>God, I can hardly see in this thing.
Ow, it's pinching my ears too.</i>

212
00:10:36,855 --> 00:10:38,649
Uh, hey, what's up?

213
00:10:40,025 --> 00:10:41,318
Nope, not you.

214
00:10:42,361 --> 00:10:44,613
Oh, that's Haruo, the new chaperone.

215
00:10:45,113 --> 00:10:46,531
- Ah, yeah?
- [Legoshi] Mmm.

216
00:10:46,615 --> 00:10:48,241
Better know the password then.

217
00:10:48,325 --> 00:10:49,368
[Legoshi] Huh?

218
00:10:49,951 --> 00:10:50,786
Uh...

219
00:10:51,495 --> 00:10:53,830
Come on, now. A hippo's skin...

220
00:10:53,914 --> 00:10:56,583
[stammers] A hippo's... skin?

221
00:10:56,667 --> 00:11:00,253
<i>Nobody told me about this! What do I do?</i>

222
00:11:03,006 --> 00:11:04,299
[indistinct chatter]

223
00:11:04,383 --> 00:11:05,342
[both] Cheers.

224
00:11:06,218 --> 00:11:09,221
- [indistinct conversation]
- [light music playing]

225
00:11:09,304 --> 00:11:12,099
[guests chattering]

226
00:11:21,108 --> 00:11:23,318
[Yahya] <i>I know Melon is here somewhere.</i>

227
00:11:24,486 --> 00:11:25,737
<i>Gazelle horns...</i>

228
00:11:26,279 --> 00:11:28,281
<i>the slender body of an herbivore...</i>

229
00:11:29,074 --> 00:11:31,368
<i>the curved back muscles of a feline...</i>

230
00:11:32,119 --> 00:11:34,454
- Careful, that tickles.
- [giggles]

231
00:11:34,538 --> 00:11:36,832
- You like it, though, don't you?
- Oh, you're such a bully.

232
00:11:37,416 --> 00:11:40,669
[guest 2] You're adorable.
Your breasts are perfect.

233
00:11:41,753 --> 00:11:42,921
[guest 1] It's my turn.

234
00:11:43,004 --> 00:11:44,714
[chattering continues]

235
00:11:45,298 --> 00:11:48,343
[Legoshi] <i>So, how are we supposed
to find him in this crowd?</i>

236
00:11:48,427 --> 00:11:50,095
[Yahya] <i>Legoshi, do you read me?</i>

237
00:11:50,846 --> 00:11:52,222
Yes, loud and clear.

238
00:11:52,931 --> 00:11:55,684
And, hey, please tell me the passwords
in advance next time.

239
00:11:56,393 --> 00:11:59,729
What? "A hippo's skin is sensitive"?
I told you that.

240
00:11:59,813 --> 00:12:01,314
[Legoshi] <i>No. No, you did not.</i>

241
00:12:01,398 --> 00:12:02,232
Well...

242
00:12:02,858 --> 00:12:05,235
Well, no harm done.
Do you have eyes on Luna?

243
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:07,863
Yes, sir.

244
00:12:08,447 --> 00:12:11,616
[Yahya] <i>Do you see the horned male
watching her? He has a glass.</i>

245
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:13,743
[Legoshi] Huh. Yeah.

246
00:12:14,578 --> 00:12:16,496
[Yahya] <i>Good.
Now look for the horned couple</i>

247
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:18,373
<i>embracing in front of the stage...</i>

248
00:12:19,541 --> 00:12:20,375
[Legoshi] Okay.

249
00:12:20,459 --> 00:12:23,211
[Yahya] <i>There's one more horned male
sitting at the bar.</i>

250
00:12:23,295 --> 00:12:26,173
<i>- He hasn't moved.</i>
- Ah. Yeah, I see him.

251
00:12:26,715 --> 00:12:29,342
<i>Melon is one of those three,
I'm sure of it.</i>

252
00:12:29,968 --> 00:12:31,678
Uh, then, how do we find out?

253
00:12:31,761 --> 00:12:33,430
[Yahya] <i>By removing their masks.</i>

254
00:12:33,513 --> 00:12:34,931
And how are we supposed to do that?

255
00:12:35,015 --> 00:12:37,142
- Well, hello there, handsome.
- [Legoshi] Huh?

256
00:12:37,225 --> 00:12:39,769
Care to join me for a little private time?

257
00:12:39,853 --> 00:12:42,063
- [Legoshi] Uh... [chuckles nervously]
- Come on.

258
00:12:42,147 --> 00:12:43,398
[both grunt]

259
00:12:43,482 --> 00:12:44,941
[guest] <i>You don't want to?</i>

260
00:12:45,025 --> 00:12:46,443
- Legoshi!
- [guest] <i>Let's go.</i>

261
00:12:46,526 --> 00:12:49,070
[Legoshi chuckling]
<i>Okay, okay. All right. You got me.</i>

262
00:12:49,154 --> 00:12:51,990
- [sighs heavily]
- [Legoshi and guest laughing]

263
00:12:55,494 --> 00:12:59,414
To think that the Beastar's office
is higher up than the mayor's is.

264
00:12:59,498 --> 00:13:01,875
- How foolish.
- What do you want?

265
00:13:02,626 --> 00:13:07,088
Lately, devouring incidents among
younger beasts have been on the rise.

266
00:13:07,923 --> 00:13:12,802
It seems that the suppressants made
by your company have lost their efficacy.

267
00:13:13,678 --> 00:13:16,723
I have to wonder
how you're spending your subsidies.

268
00:13:16,806 --> 00:13:18,767
Is that all you wanted to discuss?

269
00:13:18,850 --> 00:13:22,103
How much do you know
about the Black Market?

270
00:13:22,771 --> 00:13:26,358
It's an illicit market carnivores visit
to satisfy their needs,

271
00:13:26,441 --> 00:13:28,610
their cravings to eat fresh meat.

272
00:13:29,277 --> 00:13:31,655
It's a truly repulsive place.

273
00:13:31,738 --> 00:13:34,074
It's said that the meat sold at the market

274
00:13:34,157 --> 00:13:37,244
belonged to animals who died
in accidents or from disease.

275
00:13:38,203 --> 00:13:39,329
But, in fact...

276
00:13:41,206 --> 00:13:43,792
in the not-to-distant past,
innocent children

277
00:13:43,875 --> 00:13:47,212
were being sold there in secret
as live bait. [grunts]

278
00:13:48,213 --> 00:13:50,674
This catalogue contains records
of all those transactions.

279
00:13:50,757 --> 00:13:52,008
LIVE BAIT CATALOGUE

280
00:13:52,092 --> 00:13:54,511
And what came as the greatest shock to me,

281
00:13:54,594 --> 00:13:57,889
is that carnivores weren't the only ones
buying live meat.

282
00:13:57,973 --> 00:13:58,932
Can you imagine?

283
00:13:59,015 --> 00:14:00,058
[paper rustles]

284
00:14:00,141 --> 00:14:01,476
Here, for example.

285
00:14:02,310 --> 00:14:06,106
{\an8}This cute little fawn went
for a handsome price,

286
00:14:06,189 --> 00:14:08,149
{\an8}to another deer of all creatures!

287
00:14:08,650 --> 00:14:11,278
It's hard not to wonder if they ate him.

288
00:14:11,361 --> 00:14:12,445
[Ogma exhales]

289
00:14:14,155 --> 00:14:16,116
Now, that was 15 years ago,

290
00:14:16,199 --> 00:14:19,494
so if he were still alive,
I guess he'd be 18.

291
00:14:20,495 --> 00:14:23,206
That's the same age
as your Louis, am I right?

292
00:14:25,709 --> 00:14:27,043
Here's something funny.

293
00:14:27,127 --> 00:14:30,463
I just remembered the Black Market
has a very popular fight club.

294
00:14:31,047 --> 00:14:33,091
Their champion, Kyuu, is a young rabbit

295
00:14:33,174 --> 00:14:36,595
who somehow managed
to escape this same live bait market.

296
00:14:37,429 --> 00:14:39,639
{\an8}She may even remember that little fawn.

297
00:14:40,181 --> 00:14:41,641
{\an8}Wish that we could ask her.

298
00:14:42,434 --> 00:14:43,435
[sighs softly]

299
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:47,272
I plan to throw this in the shredder
when I finish my term.

300
00:14:47,355 --> 00:14:48,815
I have no use for it.

301
00:14:48,899 --> 00:14:52,027
It's just a relic of an unfortunate past.

302
00:14:52,110 --> 00:14:53,278
There a point to this?

303
00:14:53,737 --> 00:14:57,616
Matter of fact, there is one little thing
that I'm afraid I can only ask

304
00:14:57,699 --> 00:15:00,201
of the head of the illustrious
Horns Conglomerate.

305
00:15:01,953 --> 00:15:03,955
[both giggling]

306
00:15:06,166 --> 00:15:08,752
- [female guest] Not there. You're so bad.
- [male guest chuckles]

307
00:15:10,170 --> 00:15:11,338
[female guest giggling]

308
00:15:11,421 --> 00:15:13,006
[sniffing]

309
00:15:14,090 --> 00:15:15,008
[grunts]

310
00:15:15,091 --> 00:15:18,637
- I thought I told you no.
- I didn't. I was just looking.

311
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:21,348
He said while he was elbow deep
in the cookie jar.

312
00:15:21,431 --> 00:15:22,849
[Legoshi] Sorry. Uh...

313
00:15:23,516 --> 00:15:24,351
Oh.

314
00:15:24,935 --> 00:15:27,062
<i>Herbivores really are beautiful creatures.</i>

315
00:15:27,145 --> 00:15:27,979
[yelps]

316
00:15:28,063 --> 00:15:29,814
You better keep it in your pants, buddy.

317
00:15:29,898 --> 00:15:32,901
- I can see your mask steaming up.
- Sorry. I wasn't-- [yelps]

318
00:15:34,402 --> 00:15:35,320
[sighs]

319
00:15:36,404 --> 00:15:39,074
<i>It's so hard to breathe.
I feel like I'm going to die.</i>

320
00:15:39,157 --> 00:15:41,868
[exhales] <i>Not to mention
I can't see a thing.</i>

321
00:15:42,369 --> 00:15:44,162
<i>Eyes keep fogging up. Ow.</i>

322
00:15:45,246 --> 00:15:46,331
<i>Who would like this?</i>

323
00:15:46,414 --> 00:15:49,000
[guest] Ain't it funny how a carnivore
can wear a mask with horns

324
00:15:49,084 --> 00:15:50,752
and pretend to be an herbivore...

325
00:15:50,835 --> 00:15:53,588
[inhales sharply] ...but herbivores
who are born with them

326
00:15:53,672 --> 00:15:55,423
don't get to remove them? [scoffs]

327
00:15:56,007 --> 00:15:58,259
Pretty unfair rule,
wouldn't you say? [scoffs]

328
00:15:58,969 --> 00:16:00,637
[Legoshi] Huh? Oh, uh...

329
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:03,890
- I don't think it's that deep, buddy.
- [guest] Eh, you're right.

330
00:16:04,516 --> 00:16:05,350
[zips pants]

331
00:16:06,476 --> 00:16:07,435
Huh?

332
00:16:10,105 --> 00:16:11,147
<i>That smell...</i>

333
00:16:13,066 --> 00:16:14,067
<i>Wait, that was him!</i>

334
00:16:14,567 --> 00:16:16,736
[panting]

335
00:16:17,362 --> 00:16:19,239
[thrilling music playing]

336
00:16:22,951 --> 00:16:24,035
<i>It has to be him.</i>

337
00:16:24,536 --> 00:16:26,538
[panting]

338
00:16:27,330 --> 00:16:28,999
[thudding]

339
00:16:33,294 --> 00:16:34,129
<i>Oh.</i>

340
00:16:34,796 --> 00:16:36,006
<i>Such grace.</i>

341
00:16:36,923 --> 00:16:38,049
<i>He's beautiful.</i>

342
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:49,936
[panting]

343
00:16:52,731 --> 00:16:54,899
[exclaiming]

344
00:16:55,608 --> 00:16:56,609
<i>Oh!</i>

345
00:16:59,946 --> 00:17:02,032
[whispering] Mr. Yahya. I found Melon.

346
00:17:02,741 --> 00:17:03,950
Where is he now?

347
00:17:04,034 --> 00:17:07,537
<i>Security booth above the grid.
You can get up here from behind the bar.</i>

348
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:10,749
Got it. Do not move in until I get there.

349
00:17:10,832 --> 00:17:11,916
[Legoshi] <i>Understood.</i>

350
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:20,091
[Melon] <i>Ladies and gentlemen,
tonight we'll be serving Melda,</i>

351
00:17:20,175 --> 00:17:23,511
<i>a drink 100 times more potent
than our usual juice.</i>

352
00:17:23,595 --> 00:17:26,931
<i>Sorry, only one per person,
but, please, enjoy.</i>

353
00:17:28,892 --> 00:17:29,726
[gasps]

354
00:17:29,809 --> 00:17:31,936
[Melon] And the wolf sneaks away
from the pack

355
00:17:32,020 --> 00:17:34,147
to pick off the helpless gazelle.

356
00:17:34,856 --> 00:17:37,776
Only you're not...
You're not a pure gazelle, are you?

357
00:17:37,859 --> 00:17:39,736
- Oh?
- I could smell it.

358
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:43,323
Bodily waste, it carries the smell
of whatever you ate last.

359
00:17:43,990 --> 00:17:46,868
Your urine smelled of meat,
which wouldn't make any sense...

360
00:17:47,494 --> 00:17:48,745
if you were an herbivore.

361
00:17:48,828 --> 00:17:52,957
My, my. Nothing gets past
a canine's sense of smell, does it?

362
00:17:53,041 --> 00:17:53,917
Move!

363
00:17:58,171 --> 00:18:00,590
So, what do you want?

364
00:18:00,673 --> 00:18:01,633
To arrest you.

365
00:18:02,634 --> 00:18:04,969
- Well, not me, I just--
- Arrest me? For what?

366
00:18:05,053 --> 00:18:06,387
I haven't done anything.

367
00:18:06,888 --> 00:18:11,101
Uh... you're suspected
of the mass slaughter of large herbivores

368
00:18:11,184 --> 00:18:12,936
and illegal organ trafficking.

369
00:18:13,019 --> 00:18:13,937
Was that it?

370
00:18:14,521 --> 00:18:16,689
Anyway, my partner will be here soon.

371
00:18:16,773 --> 00:18:20,110
Hmm... You mean the horse?

372
00:18:20,193 --> 00:18:23,863
Yeah, he might be indisposed
for some time.

373
00:18:23,947 --> 00:18:25,281
But that's all right.

374
00:18:25,365 --> 00:18:27,909
What do you say we have us a little chat
until he trots in?

375
00:18:27,992 --> 00:18:29,911
- I kind of thought you'd run.
- [groans]

376
00:18:29,994 --> 00:18:32,622
Again, I haven't done anything wrong!

377
00:18:32,705 --> 00:18:35,125
[inhales sharply] Besides,
I'd love to get to know you better

378
00:18:35,208 --> 00:18:38,586
since you're not a pure wolf, are you?

379
00:18:39,295 --> 00:18:42,799
- How...
- [laughs] I knew it!

380
00:18:43,299 --> 00:18:46,636
Oh, this isn't really fair, is it?
I should take off my mask too.

381
00:18:48,012 --> 00:18:48,847
[grunts]

382
00:18:53,143 --> 00:18:54,227
Ah!

383
00:18:57,105 --> 00:19:02,110
[Legoshi] <i>It's like...
watching my own offspring hatching.</i>

384
00:19:02,694 --> 00:19:04,445
[snaps]

385
00:19:04,529 --> 00:19:08,950
Um, how did you know about me?
That I'm mixed?

386
00:19:09,033 --> 00:19:12,328
Well, first of all, you're much too big
to be a regular gray wolf,

387
00:19:12,412 --> 00:19:17,041
and, second of all, you can't seem to hide
your incredibly deep interest in me.

388
00:19:17,125 --> 00:19:19,335
- That's not what I...
- What are you mixed with?

389
00:19:19,419 --> 00:19:21,880
No, don't tell me.
It's definitely not feline.

390
00:19:22,463 --> 00:19:25,383
- Ooh, maybe a kangaroo.
- Komodo dragon, actually.

391
00:19:25,466 --> 00:19:29,137
[laughs] Really? [laughs] No way.
Your parents were freaky.

392
00:19:29,220 --> 00:19:31,931
Well, no, it's my maternal grandfather.

393
00:19:32,724 --> 00:19:36,311
<i>Wait.</i> [splutters]
<i>Why am I blabbing away like this</i>

394
00:19:36,394 --> 00:19:38,021
<i>to someone I don't even know?</i>

395
00:19:38,771 --> 00:19:40,398
Hmm. Grandfather.

396
00:19:40,481 --> 00:19:44,152
Well, my heart certainly goes out
to your poor mother. Tell her I said so.

397
00:19:44,819 --> 00:19:45,904
She's dead.

398
00:19:46,821 --> 00:19:49,949
She killed herself, uh,
when I was 12 years old.

399
00:19:50,033 --> 00:19:51,784
[inhales] Oh, my.

400
00:19:51,868 --> 00:19:54,829
I've had it pretty rough too,
my friend. I get it.

401
00:19:55,455 --> 00:19:57,081
I mean, just look at this party.

402
00:19:57,582 --> 00:20:00,251
Carnivores and herbivores
all over the world

403
00:20:00,335 --> 00:20:03,755
long to be freed
from the barriers between species,

404
00:20:03,838 --> 00:20:06,841
and here, they can drink and dance
and do just that.

405
00:20:07,425 --> 00:20:10,511
But, even that's a luxury
that we don't get.

406
00:20:11,054 --> 00:20:14,432
When you're mixed, you have no species
or comrades to speak of.

407
00:20:14,515 --> 00:20:16,684
You're just a half-baked freak of nature.

408
00:20:16,768 --> 00:20:19,812
Take that back. My mother was mixed,
but she was not a freak.

409
00:20:19,896 --> 00:20:24,150
Oh, but she was, and that's precisely why
she killed herself.

410
00:20:24,234 --> 00:20:25,443
[Legoshi] Hmm.

411
00:20:25,526 --> 00:20:29,030
A mixed beast
will always be considered a thing.

412
00:20:29,113 --> 00:20:31,449
Wait. What do you mean by that?

413
00:20:31,532 --> 00:20:33,201
Exactly what it sounds like.

414
00:20:34,118 --> 00:20:36,704
This society constantly claims
that it celebrates

415
00:20:36,788 --> 00:20:39,082
closeness between carnivores
and herbivores.

416
00:20:39,165 --> 00:20:41,501
[inhales sharply] So it's quite strange

417
00:20:41,584 --> 00:20:43,586
that whenever a child is born
from that union,

418
00:20:43,670 --> 00:20:44,712
it's an abomination.

419
00:20:44,796 --> 00:20:46,923
That's not--
I don't think of you that way.

420
00:20:47,507 --> 00:20:50,260
I think you're beautiful.
You're not an abomination.

421
00:20:50,343 --> 00:20:55,390
[scoffs] Ugh, don't tell me you're one
of those sensitive, sentimental types.

422
00:20:55,473 --> 00:20:56,766
- Huh?
- [laughs]

423
00:20:56,849 --> 00:20:59,227
There's got to be more inside of you
than that, right?

424
00:20:59,310 --> 00:21:01,104
Come on, loosen up. Tell me a joke.

425
00:21:01,187 --> 00:21:03,439
[chuckles nervously]
No, I'm not good at stuff like that.

426
00:21:03,523 --> 00:21:06,651
In that case,
I got one you're going to love.

427
00:21:06,734 --> 00:21:08,069
[suspenseful music playing]

428
00:21:08,152 --> 00:21:09,821
To think that the old stallion...

429
00:21:09,904 --> 00:21:12,365
Sorry, the world-renowned Beastar,

430
00:21:12,448 --> 00:21:15,285
<i>would recruit such a young kid
to send here in his stead...</i>

431
00:21:15,368 --> 00:21:16,661
[laughs maniacally]

432
00:21:16,744 --> 00:21:19,539
<i>Quite the little prank you pulled.
You got me good.</i>

433
00:21:19,622 --> 00:21:20,665
[growls]

434
00:21:20,748 --> 00:21:23,209
<i>But now, it's my turn.</i>

435
00:21:23,710 --> 00:21:26,838
<i>So don't touch that dial, folks,
or you'll miss the big finish.</i>

436
00:21:27,839 --> 00:21:29,882
[Legoshi breathing heavily]

437
00:21:29,966 --> 00:21:31,259
- [gun cocks]
- Legoshi!

438
00:21:31,342 --> 00:21:33,803
- [muffled gunshot]
- [Legoshi groaning]

439
00:21:33,886 --> 00:21:36,055
[Legoshi spluttering]

440
00:21:38,016 --> 00:21:39,142
<i>That was the setup.</i>

441
00:21:39,225 --> 00:21:42,312
[laughs maniacally]
<i>And now for the punchline!</i>

442
00:21:42,395 --> 00:21:44,981
[laughs maniacally]

443
00:21:45,064 --> 00:21:46,566
[all] Cheers!

444
00:21:52,196 --> 00:21:55,199
[guests screaming]

445
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

446
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,792
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

447
00:22:04,876 --> 00:22:08,212
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

448
00:22:09,422 --> 00:22:12,425
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

449
00:22:13,384 --> 00:22:15,762
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

450
00:22:17,764 --> 00:22:20,516
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

451
00:22:21,100 --> 00:22:23,644
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

452
00:22:23,728 --> 00:22:26,189
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

453
00:22:27,565 --> 00:22:31,569
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

454
00:22:32,612 --> 00:22:36,699
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

455
00:22:37,408 --> 00:22:40,078
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

456
00:22:40,161 --> 00:22:44,791
- <i>♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

457
00:22:44,874 --> 00:22:46,834
- <i>♪ Till I... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

458
00:22:46,918 --> 00:22:48,086
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

459
00:22:48,169 --> 00:22:52,423
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

460
00:22:53,216 --> 00:22:56,511
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

461
00:22:56,594 --> 00:23:00,807
- <i>♪ Just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

462
00:23:00,890 --> 00:23:02,809
- <i>♪ Till the... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

463
00:23:02,892 --> 00:23:04,268
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

464
00:23:04,852 --> 00:23:08,731
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my side ♪</i>

465
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:10,566
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

466
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,693
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

467
00:23:13,402 --> 00:23:16,405
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

468
00:23:17,448 --> 00:23:19,325
